{"name":"Sweet Baby Rose","hex":"#c24f40","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sweet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tasting of sugars.","Retaining a portion of sugar."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Used as a positive response to good news or information."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweet"},{"term":"baby","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very young human, particularly from birth to a couple of years old or until walking is fully mastered.","Any very young animal, especially a vertebrate; many species have specific names for their babies, such as kittens for the babies of cats, puppies for the babies of dogs, and chicks for the babies of birds. See Category:Baby animals for more."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Picked when small and immature (as in baby corn, baby potatoes).","Newest (overall, or in some group or state); most inexperienced."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baby"},{"term":"rose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shrub of the genus Rosa, with red, pink, white or yellow flowers.","A flower of the rose plant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make rose-colored; to redden or flush.","To perfume, as with roses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rose"}],"entries":[{"title":"Baby Rose","blocks":[{"text":"Jasmine Rose Wilson, known professionally as Baby Rose, is an American singer. As of 2026, she is signed with the record label Secretly Canadian."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baby_Rose","wikidata":"Q75197918"},{"title":"Rosa multiflora","blocks":[{"text":"Rosa multiflora is a species of rose known commonly as multiflora rose, baby rose, Japanese rose, many-flowered rose, seven-sisters rose, Eijitsu rose and rambler rose. It is native to eastern Asia, in China, Japan, and Korea. It should not be confused with Rosa rugosa, which is also known as \"Japanese rose\", or with polyantha roses which are garden cultivars derived from hybrids of R. multiflora. It was introduced to North America, where it is an invasive species, forming extensive, impenetrable stands within forest understories, thickets, borders, and lowlands. It can be identified by its characteristic fringed stipules, which form pairs at the bases of leaf stalks bearing 3–89 leaves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/2020-05-20_08_05_42_Multiflora_Rose_flowers_along_a_walking_path_within_Horsepen_Run_Stream_Valley_Park_in_Oak_Hill%2C_Fairfax_County%2C_Virginia.jpg/330px-2020-05-20_08_05_42_Multiflora_Rose_flowers_along_a_walking_path_within_Horsepen_Run_Stream_Valley_Park_in_Oak_Hill%2C_Fairfax_County%2C_Virginia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosa_multiflora","wikidata":"Q133617"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/2020-05-20_08_05_42_Multiflora_Rose_flowers_along_a_walking_path_within_Horsepen_Run_Stream_Valley_Park_in_Oak_Hill%2C_Fairfax_County%2C_Virginia.jpg/500px-2020-05-20_08_05_42_Multiflora_Rose_flowers_along_a_walking_path_within_Horsepen_Run_Stream_Valley_Park_in_Oak_Hill%2C_Fairfax_County%2C_Virginia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/2020-05-20_08_05_42_Multiflora_Rose_flowers_along_a_walking_path_within_Horsepen_Run_Stream_Valley_Park_in_Oak_Hill%2C_Fairfax_County%2C_Virginia.jpg/1280px-2020-05-20_08_05_42_Multiflora_Rose_flowers_along_a_walking_path_within_Horsepen_Run_Stream_Valley_Park_in_Oak_Hill%2C_Fairfax_County%2C_Virginia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/2020-05-20_08_05_42_Multiflora_Rose_flowers_along_a_walking_path_within_Horsepen_Run_Stream_Valley_Park_in_Oak_Hill%2C_Fairfax_County%2C_Virginia.jpg/500px-2020-05-20_08_05